{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/811148-shadows-of-abaddon","id":811148,"title":"Shadows of Abaddon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-18T08:53:20-08:00","id":811148,"title":"Shadows of Abaddon","content":"I did a game concept a long, long time ago, back when all we had for demon was Inferno. Can someone help me translate it to work in a DtD game?<br /> <br /> Here's the original thread: <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultabfc.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultabfc.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T11:10:03-08:00","id":811223,"title":"","content":"How close do you want to keep to the original material vs what you want through the lens of Descent? Do you want Descent elements included (God-Machine, Angels, etc.), themes (keeping hidden, espionage), or just harvesting the mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T11:22:43-08:00","id":811230,"title":"","content":"The mechanics? I mean, I like the embed and exploits, as well as how neat and tidy the demonic form is laid out. I even made some terminology translations, but I don't know if that's the way to go...<br /> <br /> Modifications --&gt; Mutations<br /> Technologies --&gt; Vestments<br /> Processes --&gt; Affinities <br /> Propulsion --&gt; Emanations?<br /> <br /> Analyst --&gt; Nemesis<br /> Destroyer --&gt; Slayer<br /> Guardian --&gt; Defiler<br /> Messenger --&gt; Tempter<br /> Psychopomp --&gt; Subversive<br /> <br /> Agencies<br /> Augur -- College (plural collegia)<br /> Faustian -- House<br /> Independent -- Agency<br /> Ravager -- Company<br /> Reconciler -- Chapel","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T11:38:02-08:00","id":811237,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I'm not sure about &quot;Mutations&quot;. Doesn't quite seem fitting, but I don't know.<br /> <br /> Terminology and appearance changes are fine. But what about the deeper features of Descent? Namely, the Opposition and Cover? A lot of Descent's mechanics fall apart without some overriding and pervasive threat to keep hidden from. <hr /><br /> Huh. After reading more in detail, this has a lot of similarities to a Demon project I was working on (though that one was based on Princess the Hopeful's mechanics). Convergent design. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-18-2016, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T14:14:20-08:00","id":811314,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of something similar to Cover, but singular. Actually, Torment might be a good choice to copy. But instead of high torment equaling evil, it means how much the demon is now able to sympathize with, their ability to feel compassion and/or regret. <br /> <br /> How's this: <br /> <br /> 1. Replace Cover with Torment. This represents how the infernal spirit has merged with the victim's soul, and thus has the capacity for sympathy and virtue. <br /> 2. If the demon dies, he loses a permanent dot of Torment out of 10 (which becomes 9 and so on), and must then find a new host. This represents the demon having to maintain their sanity after consuming yet another soul, each having conflicting personalities and memories. This means a given demon has a maximum of 10 &quot;lives&quot; before the Void claims him utterly.<br /> <br /> Of course, we could change the name to avoid confusion with cWoD's mechanic, if too out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T17:29:16-08:00","id":811406,"title":"","content":"Not keeping/going with Testament?<br /> <br /> And what about setting them up as serial possessors, via Pacts? In this case, a Soul Pact is &quot;here are the keys to my body/identity. Check in and out when you feel like.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, what about reducing their Power Stat by 1 (or half, or rolling for it, if you want to get aggressive) on death? That means they technically can keep coming back forever, provided they don't take too many &quot;deaths&quot; at one time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-18-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:09:23-08:00","id":811425,"title":"","content":"Testament IS the power stat, I meant to say Torment (or whatever we end up calling it) was the morality feature. Regarding the Soul Pact... I can see the potential. Almost adds a transhumanism element into the mix.<br /> <br /> With death and losing dots in Power Stat, my one fear is players getting too complacent about their Hosts dying. Then again, they still <i>TECHNICALLY</i> could if they're brought down to zero... I dunno, think it's worth a shot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 01-18-2016, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T18:47:31-08:00","id":811446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/811148-shadows-of-abaddon?p=811425#post811425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Testament IS the power stat, I meant to say Torment (or whatever we end up calling it) was the morality feature. Regarding the Soul Pact... I can see the potential. Almost adds a transhumanism element into the mix.<br /> <br /> With death and losing dots in Power Stat, my one fear is players getting too complacent about their Hosts dying. Then again, they still <i>TECHNICALLY</i> could if they're brought down to zero... I dunno, think it's worth a shot?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, my mistake with the terms.<br /> <br /> As for death consequences, you could have them roll their current Testament, then keep the successes as their new score (with Perma-Death occurring if they fail). That makes each death costly at minimum (barring them rolling nothing but successes), and potentially to end of them at maximum. Recoverable, but nothing to laugh at. Pretty brutal on XP, though. But hey - at least they aren't <i>dead</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-18-2016, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:19:37-08:00","id":811466,"title":"","content":"What happens if they roll more than their current Testament level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:25:28-08:00","id":811469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/811148-shadows-of-abaddon?p=811466#post811466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if they roll more than their current Testament level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't let them? Either negate 10-again, or just cap their Testament at their current level. Unless you want them to be able gain Testament from death. Definately brings new context to &quot;Hell and Back&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T19:35:31-08:00","id":811479,"title":"","content":"Hmm... nah, the former's less easy to game-break, although it could make for an interesting Merit or Cipher ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:17:56-08:00","id":811815,"title":"","content":"How's this for a possible mechanic?<br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:red\">Souls</span></div> <br /> A soul can be used for several different effects. One, it can be allowed to form a shade within Abaddon, granted a total number of Iliaster per day equal to Willpower, provided the harvester succeeds in tormenting it.<br /> Another option is to create a number of cacodemons (cacklings for short)--minions barely more intelligent than a five year old human--equal to dots in willpower its owner had in life. The last option is, of course, to be used for creating a Cover, as per normal. These latter options require the demon to be the rightful owner of said-soul, however, meaning either a contract with the lemure or its current master must be made first. Otherwise all attempts will immediately fail.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">Creating a Cacodemon</span><br /> As stated, the number of cacodemons that a single soul can produce is equal to the number of Willpower Dots the soul had in life. Often, a cackling reflects one of the soul's primary vices, eg; a wrathful soul will create cacklings with a penchant for violence. If the soul was known for expressing said-wrath via arson, one or more of the created cacklings might showcase signs on its person, such as being wreathed in flame, or with skin the pigment of charcoal.<br /> Beyond aesthetics, the nature of the soul should define what powers the hellspawn acquire, with all new cacodemons having at least 1 numen, embed/link, or rank in Influence. Alternatively, shards of the used soul can be fed into a single cacodemon, adding additional stats to the creature as listed below.<br /> <br /> Overview:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">\u2022 All cacodemons start at Size 1, using the stats listed under &quot;Tiny&quot;. They also acquire 1 numen determined by the ST, a link/embed from the demon creating it, or a single rank in one Influence as if it were a spirit.<br /> \u2022 If WP Dots are fed to the cacodemon, the caster may divvy them between increasing size category (resetting the cacklings attributes to match the new form)--or add an additional numen or rank in Influence (max of Rank 5) per dot. The caster can also add embeds/link or exploits/chains for equal price, but they must be ones that the demon already knows. Finally, a cackling can gain skill points from spending 1 WP (equaling 4 points worth, each), or through appropriate training.<br /> \u2022 All cacodemons have Soul Sense as a bonus power.<br /> \u2022 Cacodemons can understand any and all mundane languages, even if incapable of speech. Their Intelligence is equal to Rank, but permanently capped at 3 unless they achieve apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Tiny (Mouse, Frog, Sparrow, Lizard)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 1, Dexterity 1-3, Stamina 1<br /> Speed Factor: 1-2<br /> Size: 1<br /> Health: 2<br /> Attacks: Inflicts no real damage save maybe venom if appropriate.<br /> <br /> Small (Cat, Crow, Snake, Iguana)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 1-2, Dexterity 2-3, Stamina 1-2<br /> Speed Factor: 2-7<br /> Size: 2-3<br /> Health: 3-5<br /> Attacks: Inflicts Strength as lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Medium (Wolf, Cobra, Vulture, Monkey, Eagle)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 2-4, Dexterity 2-5, Stamina 2-4<br /> Speed Factor: 5-9<br /> Size: 4<br /> Health: 6-8<br /> Attacks: Inflicts Strength to Strength +1 (L), depending on species.<br /> <br /> Man-Sized (Cougar, Ape, Condor, Deer)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 3-6, Dexterity 3-6, Stamina 3-6<br /> Speed Factor: 5-10<br /> Size: 5-6<br /> Health: 8-12<br /> Attacks: Inflicts Strength +1 to Strength +2 (L), depending on species.<br /> <br /> Large (Horse, Bear, Dolphin, Komodo Dragon)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 4-6, Dexterity 3-5, Stamina 4-7<br /> Speed Factor: 5-12<br /> Size: 6-8<br /> Health: 10-15<br /> Attacks: Inflicts Strength +1 to Strength +3 (L); may kick or trample for Strength +3 (B).<br /> <br /> Heavy (Cattle, Moose, Bull Seal)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 4-8, Dexterity 2-4, Stamina 5-8<br /> Speed Factor: 5-10<br /> Size: 9-13<br /> Health: 14-21<br /> Attacks: Inflicts Strength +1 to Strength +3 (L); may kick or trample for Strength +3 (B).<br /> <br /> Huge (Elephant, Hippopotamus, Sea Lion, Orca)<br /> Physical Attributes: Strength 7-10, Dexterity 2-4, Stamina 7-10<br /> Speed Factor: 4-6<br /> Size: 11-15<br /> Health: 18-25<br /> Attacks: Inflicts Strength +1 to Strength +2 (L); may kick or trample for Strength +2 (B).</div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:16:04-08:00","id":811859,"title":"","content":"I would make sure to cap Cackling's maximum Rank fairly low (2, 3 at most). Being able to generate Rank 4-5 Ephemerals (even if they aren't made of ephemera, they are using the same rules) is crazy powerful.<br /> <br /> But how important is the creation of Cacodemons to the average Demon? Might this be relegated to a specific power (such as an Exploit/Chain)? Or do Demons regularly make use of swarms of these things? <hr /><br /> Just how precious/useful/hard to get are you considering Souls? Do Demon's pop them like candy and trade them like coins? Are they closely guarded resources, and traded like favors or grants of land?<br /> <br /> Do they need to track statistics other than &quot;Has Soul/Does not have Soul&quot;, such as Willpower (likely from the write-up above), Virtue/Vice, Integrity, etc.? <hr /><br /> So, a Soul's Willpower points get converted to Illiaster? I'm assuming a &quot;sustainable&quot; method of farming them is to drain Willpower, then indulge the Soul's Vice to replenish it (exploiting its Virtue takes too long, and is against theme)? Are there any ways to accelerate this at the cost of long term viability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-19-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:29:08-08:00","id":811968,"title":"","content":"Cacklings are basically cryptics here, meaning they run the gammut of minions to pets to enemies and more. That being said, souls are precious because of their utility. When you use a &quot;charge&quot;, you get a number of points equal to the soul's current WP value (which drops by 1 afterwards). Once all of it is spent, the soul disappears to parts unknown, regardless of supernatural or mundane obstructions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}